# Files / directories that must NOT enter the build context for
# Containerfile / compose.yml. Anything listed here is excluded even if a
# later COPY in the Containerfile would have asked for it — `.dockerignore`
# is checked first, before the daemon streams the context tarball.
#
# Goal: keep the build context small and free of secrets / source-control
# metadata. The runtime image only needs `package.json`, `bun.lock`,
# `tsconfig.json`, `src/`, `tmp-audio/` plus the artifacts produced by the
# `deps` and `build` stages.

# Local node_modules — never bake into the image; the `deps` stage rebuilds
# them against the slim Node base.
node_modules

# Build output — the `runtime` stage pulls `dist/` from the `build` stage,
# not from the build context.
dist

# VCS metadata and worktrees. `.worktrees/` is created by `git worktree
# add` for in-flight tickets and can balloon the build context if present.
.git
.github
.worktrees
.claude

# Runtime persisted state (gitignored). The bot writes to `data/` at
# runtime; the compose file mounts a named volume so the directory lives
# inside the container, not in the image.
data

# `.env` carries `DISCORD_TOKEN` and friends — must never be baked into a
# layer. Compose loads it via `env_file:` instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Generated / cached artifacts.
coverage
.tmp
.reference
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo

# Editor / OS noise.
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode

# Documentation and human-facing meta — not needed by the runtime image.
# Keep them out of the build context for faster `docker build` transfers.
README.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
CHANGELOG.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
SECURITY.md
docs

# The container definition itself and any override files. Compose picks them
# up from the project root, not from the image build context.
Containerfile
compose.yml
compose.*.yml
compose.*.yaml
.dockerignore